    <title>
      <narrative xml:lang="en">U.S. International Development Finance Corporation: Project Development for Argentina Potash Corporation's El Ceibo Potash Project</narrative>
    </title>
    <description type="1">
      <narrative xml:lang="en">Financing of the development phase of a Potash mine called El Ceibo in Neuquen, Argentina. The US$4.07 million DFC funding is expected to be matched dollar-for-dollar by strategic investors, resulting in total Phase 1 funding of US $8.15 million. These proceeds will advance technical studies, environmental and social impact assessments (ESIA), and pre-feasibility work, accelerating Argentina Potash Corporation's path toward construction of a 50,000 tonnes per annum (TPA) Demonstration Plant - a critical milestone on the road to full-scale commercial production of one million tonnes per annum of muriate of potash (MOP).</narrative>
    </description>
